# Caddy site file for the 27K multiplayer server on the shared box (64.177.56.111, with gifsaw,
# rnbqkbnr, csshole and the digitizer.fun games server). Installed to /etc/caddy/sites/27k.caddy by
# caddy-site.sh. The box's main /etc/caddy/Caddyfile only holds global options and
# `import /etc/caddy/sites/*.caddy`; never replace it from here.
#
# The game itself is played at ballmonitor.com/27k/ (and on itch.io); this name only answers the
# multiplayer API. Anything else is sent to the game. Automatic HTTPS: keep 27k.ballmonitor.com's
# DNS records DNS only (grey cloud) if the zone is on Cloudflare, so Caddy's HTTP challenge works.
#
# Caddy replaces X-Forwarded-For with the visitor's address (it trusts no incoming one), which the
# server's rate limit reads (TRUST_PROXY=1 in the unit).
# No per-site `log` file (`caddy validate` would create it owned by root); errors go to journalctl -u caddy.

27k.ballmonitor.com {
	@api path /api/mp/*
	handle @api {
		encode zstd gzip
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3004
	}
	handle {
		redir https://ballmonitor.com/27k/ 302
	}
}
